aseline_margin": 18.07, "analyst_adjustment": 1.93, "key_factors": ["Shapiro's incumbency and consistently strong approval in a swing state", "Polling average near +23 across high-quality pollsters", "All eight expert raters call the race Solid or Safe D", "Prediction markets price Shapiro at 97-99%"], "rationale": "Every recent poll, including those from Republican-leaning firms, shows Shapiro ahead by double digits, averaging roughly +23, and all eight raters place the race in the Safe or Solid D column. Markets price his win probability at 97% or higher, so a Safe D forecast with a margin near +20 fits the evidence.", "watch": "A late polling shift or unusually strong Republican turnout in a low-turnout midterm could narrow the margin, though not enough to threaten the outcome.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Josh Shapiro (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Pennsylvania's governor race pits incumbent Democrat Josh Shapiro against Republican state treasurer Stacy Garrity, with Libertarian Ken Krawchuk also on the ballot. Shapiro, first elected by a wide margin in 2022, has maintained strong approval ratings in a state that leans slightly Republican at the presidential level. Polls throughout the fall, from firms including Quinnipiac, Siena, Franklin & Marshall, and even Republican-leaning Susquehanna, show him ahead by 18 to 30 points.\n\nGarrity has campaigned on her military background, veterans issues, and support for skill games, with her campaign drawing millions from that industry. The race has cost more than $80 million, but outside spending has not moved the numbers. All eight expert raters call the race Solid or Safe D, and prediction markets price Shapiro's win probability at 97% or higher.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 15.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-